{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":35947857,"ns":0,"title":"Krull–Akizuki theorem","extract":"In commutative algebra, the Krull–Akizuki theorem states the following: Let A be a one-dimensional reduced noetherian ring, K its total ring of fractions. Suppose L is a finite extension of K. If \n  \n    \n      \n        A\n        ⊂\n        B\n        ⊂\n        L\n      \n    \n    {\\displaystyle A\\subset B\\subset L}\n  \n and B is reduced,\nthen B is a noetherian ring of dimension at most one.","description":"About extensions of one-dimensional Noetherian rings (commutative algebra)","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}